From e801dcaa000ad8655401c922f81f25145d27151e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucascouts <lucascs@protonmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 11:05:41 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_ui: the tasks card moves to a bar at the bottom of the
 conversation
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Zeo next proposal §6.19 (ask 39). The card's Minimize collapses it to a
floating pill with a counter and a spinner. The operator asked for what
the question card (0082) and the plan do instead: a "v" that sends it to
the bottom of the content area.

A ChevronDown in the card's header, "Move Tasks Card to the Bottom",
turns the card into a full-width bar: the pill's icon and label ("2 tasks
running", spinning while work runs) and a ChevronUp that brings the card
back, open. The bar is drawn the way the question card's bar is.

The card floats as a panel-level overlay, but the bar is not one. The
thread view on screen hosts the card entity in its own layout, in the
slot above the question card's, so the bar takes its own space instead
of covering the last entries; when both show, they stack. The panel
hands its card to each conversation view when it syncs them
(ConversationView::tasks_card), its overlay steps aside while the card
is docked, and its observation of the card also notifies the thread view
on screen, whose view is cached like the panel's. The state is kept for
the session, like minimized.

Tests: tasks_card::dock_bottom (the bar replaces the floating card and
the pill, sits above the message editor and spans the panel, and ^
brings the card back; the bar spins and is not "minimized"). Both seen
failing with set_docked_bottom made a no-op.
---

